 "title": "Sweeping PWM Pad",
 "category": "Pads and atmospheres",
 "text": "Sound: a pad that swirls and slowly opens and closes: pulse-width movement inside, a filter sweep over the top.\n\nHow it's built: a pulse whose width a slow LFO sweeps (PWM); a second, slower LFO sweeps the Ladder filter's CUTOFF over about twelve seconds; slow attack and release; Chorus and Reverb. Six voices.\n\nPlay: held chords: let it move.\n\nTweak: the two LFOs' RATEs, the filter's CV (the size of the sweep), RESONANCE.",
